{
  "id": "27885_tatsu",
  "headword": "断つ",
  "reading": "たつ",
  "romaji": "tatsu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to sever; to cut off; to give up",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to sever; to cut off; to break off; to give up",
      "explanation": "To deliberately end or break off something ongoing — a relationship, a supply, a route, or a habit. Often implies a decisive, final break."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27885_tatsu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{酒|さけ}を{断|た}つことにした。",
      "english": "I decided to give up alcohol.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27885_tatsu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}とは{連絡|れんらく}を{断|た}ったままだ。",
      "english": "I have cut off all contact with him.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27885_tatsu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{敵|てき}の{補給路|ほきゅうろ}を{断|た}つことが{作戦|さくせん}の{鍵|かぎ}だった。",
      "english": "Cutting off the enemy's supply route was the key to the operation.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}); what is severed is marked with を.\n- Pattern: [thing]を{断|た}つ\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {連絡|れんらく}を{断|た}つ: to cut off contact\n- {関係|かんけい}を{断|た}つ: to break off a relationship\n- {酒|さけ}を{断|た}つ: to give up drinking\n- {命|いのち}を{断|た}つ: to take one's own life\n\nNOTE: Written {断|た}つ for severing a connection or habit. The homophone {絶|た}つ (to end, to exterminate) overlaps closely; {裁|た}つ means to cut cloth, and {立|た}つ (00758) means to stand.",
